  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/668/668-4.htm",
  "statuteText": "668:4 Offices Voted for. –\n\nThe offices for which voters of unincorporated places are entitled to vote shall include: President and Vice-President of the United States, United States senator, United States representative, governor, executive councilor, state senator, state representative, and county offices. The voters of the unincorporated places are not entitled to vote for any town or ward offices or on any questions concerning the towns in which they vote."
